In this section, I show a test the volume fluctuation correction using Eqs. 3.6.5 within UrQMD model. Around 80 million minbias events are generated using UrQMD program (v3.4) configured as the standard cascade mode. The necessary \(N_{w}\) distribution for correction (will use \(N_{\text{part}}\) instead in following section) is from UrQMD data or a Glauber Monte Carlo simulation. For real data analysis, one has to rely on Glauber simulation to give this \(N_{\text{part}}\) distribution. In UrQMD model, \(N_{\text{part}}\) distribution can be given without Glauber model and the \(N_{\text{part}}\) distribution should be more precise than that given by the Glauber model simulation.

